.TH BLINKY-GUI 1 "2026-09-18" "blinky 1.12" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
blinky\-gui \- window for the SiPix StyleCam Blink II camera
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blinky\-gui
.SH DESCRIPTION
A front end for
.BR blinky (1).
It finds the camera, lists what is on it, downloads everything with a progress
bar and shows the five diagnostic checks, all without the terminal.
.PP
Photos already saved in the output folder appear with thumbnails. As with the
command line tool, raw camera bytes reach the disk before anything tries to
decode them.
.PP
Requires PyQt6. On Debian and Ubuntu that is the
.B python3\-pyqt6
package.
.SH "AUTOMATIC DOWNLOADING"
The window carries a tick box for the background service described under
.B watch
in
.BR blinky (1),
so it can be turned on without a terminal, and shows whether it is running.
.PP
Both cannot use the camera at once, since each would claim interface 0 and one
would fail with EBUSY. Pressing Download therefore pauses the service for the
duration and restarts it afterwards; closing the window mid-operation restarts
it as well. The window also notices the camera being plugged in or removed on
its own, so Refresh is rarely needed.
.SH RECOVERY
When a download dies partway, or the background service reports that one did,
a yellow bar appears with a
.B Recover
button. Recovery repeats what works on a failing link: download until the link
drops, unplug, plug back in, and carry on from where it stopped, until every
photo is saved. The dialog watches the bus and starts each round by itself
once the camera has been unplugged and plugged back in. Each round skips what
is already saved, by content, and stops at the first photo that will not come
through.
.PP
A round that gets nothing brings a suggestion: the kernel quirks (applied
through
.BR pkexec (1)),
then a port with fewer hubs, then another cable. Fresh batteries are never
suggested, because removing them erases the photos being recovered.
.SH UPDATING
A few seconds after opening, and twice a day after that, the window asks
GitHub whether a newer release exists, and if so shows an
.B Update
button. It downloads the package, verifies it against the release's
SHA256SUMS, and installs it with
.BR pkexec (1)
.BR apt\-get (8);
a release without checksums is refused. Set
.B BLINKY_NO_UPDATE_CHECK=1
to turn the check off.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR blinky (1)
